new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1baeadd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# L43 — interaction repair plan and delivery
+
+1. Restore canonical L42 source and preserve diary formulas/data. Done.
+2. Replace the hand-managed RAF spring driver with the existing Motion engine. Keep direct tracking, release velocity and uninterrupted current presentation. Add blur/background cancellation for navigation. Implemented; Chromium selection/drag verified. Original phone stall cause not isolated.
+3. Remove cursor-following radial light, remove width-amplified vertical skew, constrain desktop lab navigation to sidebar proportions. Implemented; vertical drag verified.
+4. Replace the experimental transformed backdrop sibling with one clipped material viewport driven by one progress spring. Original labels do not scale. Implemented; selection, Escape and immediate reopening verified in Chromium. Bounds baseline remains available; new variant stays opt-in in the lab.
+5. Add a horizontal workbench switch to exercise the same navigation controller without claiming physical iPhone emulation. Implemented; horizontal selection and drag verified in Chromium.
+6. Run TypeScript, numerical regressions and production build. Publish, save source ZIP and application patch. See VERIFICATION_L43.md.
+7. Device gate: repeat the owner's Telegram iPhone hold/reverse/background-return gesture and menu interruptions. Still open. Then decide whether to adopt the experimental menu as the default.
+
+## Material boundary
+The change removes distracting effects; it does not implement or prove native Apple Liquid Glass. Known Safari SVG-backdrop fallback remains. No WebGL renderer or hardware GPU claim is added. Further optical work needs device evidence of the actual rendering path and live backdrop deformation.
