--- /dev/null
+++ b/VERIFICATION_L43.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# L43 evidence
+
+Passed: TypeScript; ten numerical regression tests (including legacy menu math, not a new-driver device test); Chromium preview navigation selection, rapid retargeting, vertical drag, horizontal drag, menu selection, Escape and immediate reopening after selecting a menu item. Read-only DOM observations confirmed the settled lens at the selected target and an overflow-hidden menu with no sibling backdrop shell.
+
+Implemented beyond that observed set: navigation cancels an active gesture on browser blur or document hiding. Background-return and physical touch remain unverified. No new physical iPhone acceptance, interaction video or GPU performance measurement was produced. No exact diagnosis of the original phone stall is claimed.
+
+Production defaults: shared spring scheduling and restrained light/shape repairs apply to existing consumers. Experimental menu remains opt-in in /interaction-lab. Diary data, formulas and workout entry remain unchanged. Desktop workbench offers a horizontal layout switch; this is not iPhone emulation.
